Q-Audion runtime tuning API (rtc_base/qaudion_tuning.{h,cc}) plus the GN,
Android JNI and ObjC wiring that exposes it.

New process-wide, lock-free API that P4b, P5 (this author) and P6, P7 (the
crypto author) all call into:
- SetOpusEncoderComplexity/OpusEncoderComplexity: 0..10 or -1 (build
  default), mid-call changes allowed.
- SetOpusDecoderComplexity/OpusDecoderComplexity (finding #15): 0..10 or -1
  (kQaudionDefaultDecoderComplexity = 7 for now; only 5/6/7 currently change
  libopus behavior - deep PLC / OSCE LACE / OSCE NoLACE).
- SetOpusMinPacketLossPercent/OpusMinPacketLossPercent: FEC floor, default
  10, clamped 0..20.
- SetRequireDtlsPqc/RequireDtlsPqc: tighten-only for the life of the
  process.
- RaiseTransportLevel/TransportLevel: 0..3, raise-only, no-op (always 3) in
  QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT builds.
- DisableMagicBytesBypass/MagicBytesBypassAllowed (finding #13, name not in
  the plan - picked to match the existing tighten-only naming; reconciled by
  the integrator against the crypto author's P1 amendment, which calls
  qaudion::MagicBytesBypassAllowed() directly): tighten-only, always false in
  QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT builds. [Integrator, stage 2: this patch's own
  first draft named the getter MagicBytesBypassDisabled(); P1 was written
  independently against MagicBytesBypassAllowed(). Renamed here (and
  inverted the boolean) to the one name both patches now use, since P1 must
  stay untouched (its line numbers are shared with P2/P3, applied earlier in
  the series). DisableMagicBytesBypass() itself was already spelled
  identically in both patches and needed no change.]
- TuningGeneration: bumped once per setter call that actually changed a
  stored value; P4b/P5 poll it instead of taking a lock or a callback.
- BuildInfo: ids/booleans/small integers only, safe for telemetry.

Safety: every stored value lives in its own std::atomic<>; every setter
range-checks (and, where -1 is not a valid sentinel, clamps) its input
before storing, so no argument - including one the app derived from a
remote flag or SDP attribute - can reach an RTC_CHECK, an out-of-range
libopus CTL, or a BoringSSL call. No RTC_CHECK anywhere in this file
(grepped). The four "tighten-only" knobs (PQC requirement, transport level,
magic-bytes bypass) have no path back to a looser state short of a process
restart, and QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT builds hard-wire the tightest setting
regardless of whether the setter was ever called.

QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT is a single macro propagated through //:common_config
(root BUILD.gn) from one new GN arg, rtc_qaudion_transport_strict
(webrtc.gni; default true = plain/strict). common_config is one of
rtc_add_configs, applied by webrtc.gni's set_defaults() to every
rtc_library/rtc_source_set/rtc_static_library/rtc_executable/rtc_shared_library/
rtc_test target's own `configs` - not just to dependents via public_configs,
so every translation unit built by these templates gets the define directly,
with no dependency-graph gap possible. [Integrator, stage 2: this paragraph
originally said "//:common_inherited_config"; the diff below actually edits
`config("common_config")`, confirmed against the pinned root BUILD.gn (the
"rtc_use_perfetto" context the hunk below is anchored to sits inside that
config, not common_inherited_config). Corrected the prose to match the code;
no behavior changes; common_config's reach turned out to be a superset of
what common_inherited_config would have given here, since it does not rely
on any target remembering to depend on qaudion_tuning to inherit the define -
see the integrator's dep-wiring notes for why several targets needed an
explicit qaudion_tuning dep for the *symbols*, which is a separate, narrower
requirement than seeing the macro.] qaudion_tuning.h #errors out at compile
time if a target somehow still didn't see the define, instead of silently
linking in a stale per-file default. New rtc_base
target `qaudion_tuning` (rtc_base/BUILD.gn) is added to the deps of
modules/audio_coding:webrtc_opus, the sdk/android peerconnection_jni target
and sdk:peerconnection_objc; api/crypto:options and the ssl_adapter target
are the crypto author's to wire (P6/P7 call into this API too, per the plan,
but I did not touch api/crypto/BUILD.gn or the ssl_adapter deps list -
report to the integrator if `git apply --check` for P6/P7 complains about a
missing qaudion_tuning dep there).

Android surface: five setters, a raise, a disable, and a getter added to
the existing org.webrtc.PeerConnectionFactory class (no new files - the
LiveKit build's package-prefixing pipeline (build/patches/jni_prefix.patch)
therefore applies to this the same as every other method already there).
JNI bridges follow the exact naming/pattern of the neighboring
JNI_PeerConnectionFactory_InitializeFieldTrials (jni_zero-generated; this
M150 revision still uses the legacy JNI_ClassName_MethodName convention for
the C++ side even though parameters are jni_zero types).

ObjC surface: the same seven as class methods on
RTC_OBJC_TYPE(RTCPeerConnectionFactory), so the LiveKit build's
apple_prefix.patch turns them into LKRTCPeerConnectionFactory automatically,
same as every other selector on that interface.

Finding #14 (partial - the ObjC half; RecreateEncoderInstance's
generation-read-ordering half is fixed in P5): NSInteger is 64-bit on
arm64, so every value crossing into the 32-bit `int` the C++ API takes is
explicitly clamped in the .mm (QaudionClampNSInteger), not just narrowed -
an out-of-range NSInteger would otherwise truncate instead of hitting
qaudion_tuning's own range check. The clamp range for the two complexity
setters is [-1, 10], not [0, 10], because -1 ("build default") is part of
their valid domain.

Order: 4th in the series (m150/series), right after P1/P2/P3 and before
P4a/P4b/P5/P6/P7 - all five of the latter depend on this API or its GN
target.

Touches (all in dir "."): webrtc.gni, BUILD.gn, rtc_base/BUILD.gn,
modules/audio_coding/BUILD.gn, sdk/android/BUILD.gn, sdk/BUILD.gn,
sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/PeerConnectionFactory.java,
sdk/android/src/jni/pc/peer_connection_factory.cc,
sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCPeerConnectionFactory.{h,mm}; new files
rtc_base/qaudion_tuning.{h,cc}.

Verified: `git apply --check` and a real apply are clean against the
pinned, partial webrtc-sdk/webrtc @ ba469aa2093ba950066258ca0a59a6fbd1295582
checkout, on top of P1 + P2 + P3 already applied, in series order. All
touched symbols (JNI_PeerConnectionFactory_InitializeFieldTrials's exact
signature and jni_zero calling convention, NSString+StdString's
`+stringForStdString:`, the webrtc_opus/peerconnection_jni/peerconnection_objc
target names and their existing rtc_base: deps, common_inherited_config's
location in the root BUILD.gn) were read from that same pinned checkout,
not assumed.

